Print the metadata budget of every chunk request

A three page request in the pointer range cannot get a chunk even though the
metadata claim is a hundred megabytes, so print how many slots the range owns, how
many the request wants and the total budget.  That separates a range divided to zero
from a size class asking for the wrong number of slots.
---
diff --git a/osfmk/vm/vm_kern.c b/osfmk/vm/vm_kern.c
index 2927d4b..2ed9250 100644
--- a/osfmk/vm/vm_kern.c
+++ b/osfmk/vm/vm_kern.c
@@ -2844,6 +2844,12 @@ kmem_get_new_chunk(
 		meta = from_right ? metab : metaf;
 		meta_num = kmem_get_additional_meta(meta, meta_req, from_right,
 		    &adj_free_meta);
+		/*
+		 * nio: a three page request cannot get a chunk, so print what the range
+		 * owns, what this request wants and the total metadata budget.
+		 */
+		printf("\nM r=%d num=%u span=%ld barea=%#llx", range_id, meta_num,
+		    (long)(metab - metaf), (unsigned long long)kmem_meta_size);
 
 		if (metaf + meta_num >= metab) {
 			kmem_range_out_of_va(range_id, meta_num);
